at last Mario Kart 8 returns with the  deluxe edition complete with every  single track from the original plus a  few extras thrown in veterans of the  series will feel right at home with the  game but for all you switch owners out  there who are new to it and haven't  quite discovered all the alternate paths  in the courses we've got for you the  eight shortcuts that will change the way  you race in Mario Kart 8 forever now if  you haven't picked up the game yet go  watch our video review buy games plus  own Cali play II buy it and wait  patiently for the mailman to come ok you  ready let's do this  [Music]  we'll start off with the Wii U version  of Rainbow Road because why not after  jumping the first gap onto the red and  green conveyor belts make sure you board  the next ramp on the right side from  there you'll have a straight shot for  this shortcut look for the turn after  the spin boost pillar and drive off the  course to the left side and you should  land on the alternate track underneath  now keep driving and leap off this ledge  back onto the original track and if all  goes according to plan you will have  shaved a couple seconds off your time  and hopefully be in good position to  take first place  [Music]  this one's a little bit simpler but it  can be just as risky cloudtop cruz has  you bouncing around in the sky but if  you dare you can take the shortcut right  at the very end of course  see those two leaves poking out from the  Beanstalk make a hard right after  landing on this section and you'll be  able to jump on to them and straight to  the finish line but if you're looking  for an even better finishing shortcut  well  both of these courses feature some of  the most treacherous shortcuts out there  and both are right before their final  turns in shy guy falls after you fly off  the waterfall keep a lookout on the  right side for a narrow grassy road  you'll need to use a mushroom to boost  through it and make the jump but make  sure you drift right away to avoid  flying off the left side after you land  and same goes for mute city the ramp is  a little more hidden but take a right  here and you'll be treated to a nice  relaxing jump that ends in the checkered  flag  [Music]  ah yes Hyrule Castle has its own course  in Mario Kart 8 deluxe and it comes with  an awesome-looking shortcut right in the  center of the castle there's a good  chance you'll need the help of some of  the other racers to activate it but once  you hit all the spin boost pillars on  the stairs a ramp will open up for you  and anyone else nearby to use it may not  save you the most time but there's  arguably nothing cooler than jumping  straight through the Master Sword but if  you're looking for some massive  time-saving jumps that'll bump you up a  couple places in the standings try  ribbon roads to shortcuts take a right  as soon as you board the floating ribbon  portion of the track and jump over the  giant toy bear then immediately take  another right to hit this ramp and float  into the final turn these shortcuts are  riskier than most but when everyone is  bouncing around trying to drip those  turns  you'll be gliding comfortably into first  place  [Music]  technically speaking yoshi Valley has no  shortcuts instead there are multiple  roads that branch off from each other  meaning there are a bunch of different  ways that you can complete the course  but which path should you take well  there is an optimal path to follow and  it goes like this on the first fork in  the road make a left and then continue  making the left until you reach that  narrow wooden bridge once you cross it  you should be in good position to take  first place or get hit by a red shell  both outcomes are equally likely  [Music]  Mountain Wario is one of the most  competitive and rage-inducing courses  out there you'll have to make your way  from the summit of the mountain down to  the base all while avoiding cliffs  dodging trees and dealing with all sorts  of BS power-ups along the way but if you  want to separate yourself from the crowd  try these two shortcuts in the first  area of the course there are a few  hairpin turns that you'll need to watch  out for but during the curve right  before the cave entrance you can drift a  little early hop off the small ramp and  cut the turnout completely the second  short cut is a little more hidden and  you'll need a mushroom for it but it's  well worth the effort after the section  with the dam you'll come to another fork  in the road you can go left you can go  right but instead we're going straight  boost through the snow right here and  you'll be treated with a jump that will  bypass some of the trickier turns  through the forest an honorable mention  goes to ice ice outpost because despite  the course having two alternate paths  that will save you a lot of time the low  friction and narrow ramps just make the  shortcuts way too risky to recommend  I would say not to waste your energy on  it and just concentrate on dealing with  the courses slippery roads instead so  those are our picks for the eight best  shortcuts in Mario Kart 8 plus one that  you probably should just avoid if you  have a favorite way of getting ahead of  the pack of aside from a blue shell of  course posting in the comments below and  then we can argue about it because what  is Mario Kart if not unadulterated rage  and fury  my name is Joey and thanks for watching  [Music]
 

